# The pelt tree PAX runs as PID 1 (px13; tools/mkpelt builds it).
#
# pelt trunk at the time of px13 (2026-10-08): dd22a86 (sh02, the
# prompt: pelt is interactive, reads standard input byte-wise, prompts
# with PS1 and PS2 on standard error), pinned in its own
# wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf 0.2.24 / lupin 0.1.47 / wolf-std
# 2f389a7. tools/mkpelt builds it with THAT toolchain (the archive by
# the digest pelt names, the std tree at the commit it names), not with
# kernel/wolf.pin's: the binary is pelt's own, built from pelt's own
# tree, as tools/mkboreutils builds boreutils.
#
# px17 (2026-10-09) moves it to pelt trunk 3e7516c (sh03, H2: pipelines,
# every redirection form, `cd`, `&` and `wait`, command substitutions
# that run programs), pinned in its own wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf
# 0.2.26 / lupin 0.1.49 / wolf-std 2f389a7.
#
# px26 (2026-10-11) moves it to pelt trunk b32bebc (sh05: `exec`,
# `unset`, `trap`, and Ctrl-C as a signal), pinned in its own
# wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf 0.2.27 / lupin 0.1.50. This pelt starts a
# second thread before its first prompt (wolf's runtime listens for
# signals there) and waits on futexes, so it runs only on a kernel with
# threads, futexes and signals delivered: px26's.
#
# px46 (2026-10-15) moves it to pelt trunk 7dd3304 (sh15), pinned in its
# own wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf 0.2.30 / lupin 0.1.53 / wolf-std
# fd6bcdc: sh11's line editor (pelt owns the terminal: raw mode and its
# own echo), sh12's history (`$HOME/.sh_history`), sh13's `umask`,
# sh14's `kill` and `trap` for every signal, sh15's terminal (the
# window's size, the special characters, a prompt that waits on
# `os_signal_wait_fd` instead of a timed read).
#
# px47 (2026-10-16) moves it to pelt trunk 06223a8 (sh16: tab
# completion of commands, files and variables, a second Tab lists),
# the same wolf-toolchain.toml as 7dd3304. tools/mkpelt links it with
# ld.lld (px13-ubuntu and CI have it); sh16's own static build had no
# ld.lld on PATH, so wolf linked with the system linker and its binary
# (6774441b…) is not this one (notes/px47).
#
# px49 (2026-10-17) moves it to pelt 1102498 (sh17, pelt#31; trunk
# c435b9a adds notes only after it): option clusters and `--`, aliases,
# a command table with `hash`, `type` and `command -v -V -p`, `$'…'`, a
# real `pipefail`, `read`'s corners; the same wolf-toolchain.toml as
# 06223a8. sh17 built it with this tools/mkpelt (pax 5c36560's, the same
# file as 6d4072c's) to 07bb5156… (15,047,176 bytes).
#
# px51 (2026-10-18) moves it to pelt 2676879 (sh18, H3e; trunk cc2fdc9
# adds notes only after it): job control, on by default when
# interactive (`set -m`): the shell leads a group and takes the
# terminal, each top-level pipeline is a job in a group of its own given
# the terminal in the foreground, `jobs`, `fg`, `bg`, job ids, notices,
# `kill` to a job's group; new calls `setpgid` and `getpgrp`. Its own
# wolf-toolchain.toml moves to wolf 0.2.32 / lupin 0.1.54 / wolf-std
# d37c911. sh18 built it with this tools/mkpelt (pax b274030's) to
# 76f3fc40… (15,198,832 bytes).
#
# px53 (2026-10-20) moves it to pelt be1a75d (trunk: sh19's 110ba56,
# then tl28's CI; src/ is cd05c3b's): #33's leak (the ordinary path's
# scratch freed each turn), #35, and #37 (`cd`'s relative join adds a
# `/` only when the base does not end in one: `cd bin` from `/` is
# `/bin`). The same wolf-toolchain.toml (wolf 0.2.32 / lupin 0.1.54 /
# wolf-std d37c911: pelt's 0.2.33 pin is sh20's); the same 50 calls by
# name. sh19 built cd05c3b with pax d6fbcdc's tools/mkpelt (this file's
# since) to 7be05ec0… (15,200,336 bytes).
PELT_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/pelt
